{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Find the startup wait with strace",
  "hook": "How do you use `strace -f -T -e trace=` to find why a program hangs on startup?",
  "topic": "os/process/strace-syscall-tracing",
  "tags": [
    "os",
    "strace",
    "linux"
  ],
  "level": "intermediate",
  "series": "os-syscalls-and-processes",
  "series_index": 1,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "A launcher may be waiting while its child is doing the real work.",
      "narration": "Your service hangs before its first log line. Trace the launch with child following enabled, elapsed syscall timing, and a focused syscall filter.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Trace the children",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "inspect",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sh",
          "text": "strace -f -T -yy \\\n  -e trace=network,read,poll,futex \\\n  -o startup.trace ./server",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 34,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "checks",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "-f follows child processes",
            "-T times completed syscalls"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 64,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 24,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 3400,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "A long poll shows waiting, not necessarily the root cause.",
      "narration": "Suppose the trace shows a poll returning after five seconds. That proves a wait, not a slow CPU loop; inspect the descriptor and surrounding calls.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Read the evidence",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "inspect",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "trace",
          "text": "# Illustrative excerpt; fd varies\npoll([{fd=7, events=POLLIN}],\n     1, 5000) = 0 (Timeout)\n     <5.005123>",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 34,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "checks",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "An unfinished call has no final -T yet",
            "Use -yy to decode descriptor details"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 64,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 24,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 3400,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "The syscall boundary connects the symptom to a resource.",
      "narration": "For a still running process, inspect the descriptor through proc. A socket points toward a network dependency; a futex suggests synchronization, requiring thread stacks.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Map the descriptor",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "inspect",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sh",
          "text": "readlink /proc/1234/fd/7\nss -tnp\n# Replace 1234 with the traced PID",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 34,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "checks",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Match PID and descriptor lifetime",
            "A futex wait alone does not prove deadlock"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 64,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 24,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 3400,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "Repeat the same startup path after fixing the dependency.",
      "narration": "Fix the demonstrated dependency, then repeat the same capture. Compare waits and startup time; strace adds overhead and cannot explain every user space stall.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Confirm the repair",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "node0",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "Blocked syscall → dependency",
